#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-send-email(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:7
msgid "git-send-email - Send a collection of patches as emails"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:16
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t'git send-email' [<options>] (<file>|<directory>)...\n"
"\t'git send-email' [<options>] <format-patch-options>\n"
"\t'git send-email' --dump-aliases\n"
"\t'git send-email' --translate-aliases\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:26
msgid ""
"Takes the patches given on the command line and emails them out.  Patches "
"can be specified as files, directories (which will send all files in the "
"directory), or directly as a revision list.  In the last case, any format "
"accepted by linkgit:git-format-patch[1] can be passed to git send-email, as "
"well as options understood by linkgit:git-format-patch[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:30
msgid ""
"The header of the email is configurable via command-line options.  If not "
"specified on the command line, the user will be prompted with a ReadLine "
"enabled interface to provide the necessary information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:32
msgid "There are two formats accepted for patch files:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:34
msgid "mbox format files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:37
msgid ""
"This is what linkgit:git-format-patch[1] generates.  Most headers and MIME "
"formatting are ignored."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:40
msgid ""
"The original format used by Greg Kroah-Hartman's 'send_lots_of_email.pl' "
"script"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:43
msgid ""
"This format expects the first line of the file to contain the \"Cc:\" value "
"and the \"Subject:\" of the message as the second line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:49
#, no-wrap
msgid "Composing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:55
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--annotate::`\n"
"\tReview and edit each patch you're about to send. Default is the value\n"
"\tof `sendemail.annotate`. See the CONFIGURATION section for\n"
"\t`sendemail.multiEdit`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:59
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--bcc=<address>,...::`\n"
"\tSpecify a \"Bcc:\" value for each email. Default is the value of\n"
"\t`sendemail.bcc`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:61
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:67
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:130
msgid "This option may be specified multiple times."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:65
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--cc=<address>,...::`\n"
"\tSpecify a starting \"Cc:\" value for each email.\n"
"\tDefault is the value of `sendemail.cc`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:71
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--compose::`\n"
"\tInvoke a text editor (see GIT_EDITOR in linkgit:git-var[1])\n"
"\tto edit an introductory message for the patch series.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:78
msgid ""
"When `--compose` is used, git send-email will use the From, To, Cc, Bcc, "
"Subject, Reply-To, and In-Reply-To headers specified in the message. If the "
"body of the message (what you type after the headers and a blank line) only "
"contains blank (or Git: prefixed) lines, the summary won't be sent, but the "
"headers mentioned above will be used unless they are removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:80
msgid "Missing From or In-Reply-To headers will be prompted for."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:82
msgid "See the CONFIGURATION section for `sendemail.multiEdit`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:90
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--from=<address>::`\n"
"\tSpecify the sender of the emails.  If not specified on the command line,\n"
"\tthe value of the `sendemail.from` configuration option is used.  If\n"
"\tneither the command-line option nor `sendemail.from` are set, then the\n"
"\tuser will be prompted for the value.  The default for the prompt will be\n"
"\tthe value of GIT_AUTHOR_IDENT, or GIT_COMMITTER_IDENT if that is not\n"
"\tset, as returned by \"git var -l\".\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:95
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--reply-to=<address>::`\n"
"\tSpecify the address where replies from recipients should go to.\n"
"\tUse this if replies to messages should go to another address than what\n"
"\tis specified with the --from parameter.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:102
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--in-reply-to=<identifier>::`\n"
"\tMake the first mail (or all the mails with `--no-thread`) appear as a\n"
"\treply to the given Message-ID, which avoids breaking threads to\n"
"\tprovide a new patch series.\n"
"\tThe second and subsequent emails will be sent as replies according to\n"
"\tthe `--[no-]chain-reply-to` setting.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:106
msgid ""
"So for example when `--thread` and `--no-chain-reply-to` are specified, the "
"second and subsequent patches will be replies to the first one like in the "
"illustration below where `[PATCH v2 0/3]` is in reply to `[PATCH 0/2]`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:114
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  [PATCH 0/2] Here is what I did...\n"
"    [PATCH 1/2] Clean up and tests\n"
"    [PATCH 2/2] Implementation\n"
"    [PATCH v2 0/3] Here is a reroll\n"
"      [PATCH v2 1/3] Clean up\n"
"      [PATCH v2 2/3] New tests\n"
"      [PATCH v2 3/3] Implementation\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:117
msgid ""
"Only necessary if --compose is also set.  If --compose is not set, this will "
"be prompted for."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:122
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--subject=<string>::`\n"
"\tSpecify the initial subject of the email thread.\n"
"\tOnly necessary if --compose is also set.  If --compose\n"
"\tis not set, this will be prompted for.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:128
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--to=<address>,...::`\n"
"\tSpecify the primary recipient of the emails generated. Generally, this\n"
"\twill be the upstream maintainer of the project involved. Default is the\n"
"\tvalue of the `sendemail.to` configuration value; if that is unspecified,\n"
"\tand --to-cmd is not specified, this will be prompted for.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:137
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--8bit-encoding=<encoding>::`\n"
"\tWhen encountering a non-ASCII message or subject that does not\n"
"\tdeclare its encoding, add headers/quoting to indicate it is\n"
"\tencoded in <encoding>.  Default is the value of the\n"
"\t'sendemail.assume8bitEncoding'; if that is unspecified, this\n"
"\twill be prompted for if any non-ASCII files are encountered.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:139
msgid "Note that no attempts whatsoever are made to validate the encoding."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:143
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--compose-encoding=<encoding>::`\n"
"\tSpecify encoding of compose message. Default is the value of the\n"
"\t'sendemail.composeEncoding'; if that is unspecified, UTF-8 is assumed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:152
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--transfer-encoding=(7bit|8bit|quoted-printable|base64|auto)::`\n"
"\tSpecify the transfer encoding to be used to send the message over SMTP.\n"
"\t7bit will fail upon encountering a non-ASCII message.  quoted-printable\n"
"\tcan be useful when the repository contains files that contain carriage\n"
"\treturns, but makes the raw patch email file (as saved from a MUA) much\n"
"\tharder to inspect manually.  base64 is even more fool proof, but also\n"
"\teven more opaque.  auto will use 8bit when possible, and "
"quoted-printable\n"
"\totherwise.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:155
msgid ""
"Default is the value of the `sendemail.transferEncoding` configuration "
"value; if that is unspecified, default to `auto`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:161
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--xmailer::`\n"
"`--no-xmailer::`\n"
"\tAdd (or prevent adding) the \"X-Mailer:\" header.  By default,\n"
"\tthe header is added, but it can be turned off by setting the\n"
"\t`sendemail.xmailer` configuration variable to `false`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:163
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sending"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:173
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--envelope-sender=<address>::`\n"
"\tSpecify the envelope sender used to send the emails.\n"
"\tThis is useful if your default address is not the address that is\n"
"\tsubscribed to a list. In order to use the 'From' address, set the\n"
"\tvalue to \"auto\". If you use the sendmail binary, you must have\n"
"\tsuitable privileges for the -f parameter.  Default is the value of the\n"
"\t`sendemail.envelopeSender` configuration variable; if that is\n"
"\tunspecified, choosing the envelope sender is left to your MTA.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:181
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--sendmail-cmd=<command>::`\n"
"\tSpecify a command to run to send the email. The command should\n"
"\tbe sendmail-like; specifically, it must support the `-i` option.\n"
"\tThe command will be executed in the shell if necessary.  Default\n"
"\tis the value of `sendemail.sendmailCmd`.  If unspecified, and if\n"
"\t--smtp-server is also unspecified, git-send-email will search\n"
"\tfor `sendmail` in `/usr/sbin`, `/usr/lib` and $PATH.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:195
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--smtp-encryption=<encryption>::`\n"
"\tSpecify in what way encrypting begins for the SMTP connection.\n"
"\tValid values are 'ssl' and 'tls'. Any other value reverts to plain\n"
"\t(unencrypted) SMTP, which defaults to port 25.\n"
"\tDespite the names, both values will use the same newer version of TLS,\n"
"\tbut for historic reasons have these names. 'ssl' refers to \"implicit\"\n"
"\tencryption (sometimes called SMTPS), that uses port 465 by default.\n"
"\t'tls' refers to \"explicit\" encryption (often known as STARTTLS),\n"
"\tthat uses port 25 by default. Other ports might be used by the SMTP\n"
"\tserver, which are not the default. Commonly found alternative port for\n"
"\t'tls' and unencrypted is 587. You need to check your provider's\n"
"\tdocumentation or your server configuration to make sure\n"
"\tfor your own case. Default is the value of `sendemail.smtpEncryption`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:202
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--smtp-domain=<FQDN>::`\n"
"\tSpecifies the Fully Qualified Domain Name (FQDN) used in the\n"
"\tHELO/EHLO command to the SMTP server.  Some servers require the\n"
"\tFQDN to match your IP address.  If not set, git send-email attempts\n"
"\tto determine your FQDN automatically.  Default is the value of\n"
"\t`sendemail.smtpDomain`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:206
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--smtp-auth=<mechanisms>::`\n"
"\tWhitespace-separated list of allowed SMTP-AUTH mechanisms. This setting\n"
"\tforces using only the listed mechanisms. Example:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:209
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ git send-email --smtp-auth=\"PLAIN LOGIN GSSAPI\" ...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:217
msgid ""
"If at least one of the specified mechanisms matches the ones advertised by "
"the SMTP server and if it is supported by the utilized SASL library, the "
"mechanism is used for authentication. If neither 'sendemail.smtpAuth' nor "
"`--smtp-auth` is specified, all mechanisms supported by the SASL library can "
"be used. The special value 'none' maybe specified to completely disable "
"authentication independently of `--smtp-user`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:223
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--smtp-pass[=<password>]::`\n"
"\tPassword for SMTP-AUTH. The argument is optional: If no\n"
"\targument is specified, then the empty string is used as\n"
"\tthe password. Default is the value of `sendemail.smtpPass`,\n"
"\thowever `--smtp-pass` always overrides this value.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:229
msgid ""
"Furthermore, passwords need not be specified in configuration files or on "
"the command line. If a username has been specified (with `--smtp-user` or a "
"`sendemail.smtpUser`), but no password has been specified (with "
"`--smtp-pass` or `sendemail.smtpPass`), then a password is obtained using "
"'git-credential'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:232
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--no-smtp-auth::`\n"
"\tDisable SMTP authentication. Short hand for `--smtp-auth=none`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:239
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--smtp-server=<host>::`\n"
"\tIf set, specifies the outgoing SMTP server to use (e.g.\n"
"\t`smtp.example.com` or a raw IP address).  If unspecified, and if\n"
"\t`--sendmail-cmd` is also unspecified, the default is to search\n"
"\tfor `sendmail` in `/usr/sbin`, `/usr/lib` and $PATH if such a\n"
"\tprogram is available, falling back to `localhost` otherwise.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:245
msgid ""
"For backward compatibility, this option can also specify a full pathname of "
"a sendmail-like program instead; the program must support the `-i` option.  "
"This method does not support passing arguments or using plain command "
"names.  For those use cases, consider using `--sendmail-cmd` instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:253
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--smtp-server-port=<port>::`\n"
"\tSpecifies a port different from the default port (SMTP\n"
"\tservers typically listen to smtp port 25, but may also listen to\n"
"\tsubmission port 587, or the common SSL smtp port 465);\n"
"\tsymbolic port names (e.g. \"submission\" instead of 587)\n"
"\tare also accepted. The port can also be set with the\n"
"\t`sendemail.smtpServerPort` configuration variable.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:258
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--smtp-server-option=<option>::`\n"
"\tIf set, specifies the outgoing SMTP server option to use.\n"
"\tDefault value can be specified by the `sendemail.smtpServerOption`\n"
"\tconfiguration option.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:262
msgid ""
"The --smtp-server-option option must be repeated for each option you want to "
"pass to the server. Likewise, different lines in the configuration files "
"must be used for each option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:265
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--smtp-ssl::`\n"
"\tLegacy alias for '--smtp-encryption ssl'.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:276
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--smtp-ssl-cert-path::`\n"
"\tPath to a store of trusted CA certificates for SMTP SSL/TLS\n"
"\tcertificate validation (either a directory that has been processed\n"
"\tby 'c_rehash', or a single file containing one or more PEM format\n"
"\tcertificates concatenated together: see verify(1) -CAfile and\n"
"\t-CApath for more information on these). Set it to an empty string\n"
"\tto disable certificate verification. Defaults to the value of the\n"
"\t`sendemail.smtpSSLCertPath` configuration variable, if set, or the\n"
"\tbacking SSL library's compiled-in default otherwise (which should\n"
"\tbe the best choice on most platforms).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:281
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--smtp-user=<user>::`\n"
"\tUsername for SMTP-AUTH. Default is the value of `sendemail.smtpUser`;\n"
"\tif a username is not specified (with `--smtp-user` or "
"`sendemail.smtpUser`),\n"
"\tthen authentication is not attempted.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:286
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--smtp-debug=(0|1)::`\n"
"\tEnable (1) or disable (0) debug output. If enabled, SMTP\n"
"\tcommands and replies will be printed. Useful to debug TLS\n"
"\tconnection and authentication problems.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:296
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--batch-size=<num>::`\n"
"\tSome email servers (e.g. smtp.163.com) limit the number emails to be\n"
"\tsent per session (connection) and this will lead to a failure when\n"
"\tsending many messages.  With this option, send-email will disconnect "
"after\n"
"\tsending $<num> messages and wait for a few seconds (see --relogin-delay)\n"
"\tand reconnect, to work around such a limit.  You may want to\n"
"\tuse some form of credential helper to avoid having to retype\n"
"\tyour password every time this happens.  Defaults to the\n"
"\t`sendemail.smtpBatchSize` configuration variable.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:301
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--relogin-delay=<int>::`\n"
"\tWaiting $<int> seconds before reconnecting to SMTP server. Used together\n"
"\twith --batch-size option.  Defaults to the `sendemail.smtpReloginDelay`\n"
"\tconfiguration variable.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:303
#, no-wrap
msgid "Automating"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:310
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--no-to::`\n"
"`--no-cc::`\n"
"`--no-bcc::`\n"
"\tClears any list of \"To:\", \"Cc:\", \"Bcc:\" addresses previously\n"
"\tset via config.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:314
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--no-identity::`\n"
"\tClears the previously read value of `sendemail.identity` set\n"
"\tvia config, if any.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:320
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--to-cmd=<command>::`\n"
"\tSpecify a command to execute once per patch file which\n"
"\tshould generate patch file specific \"To:\" entries.\n"
"\tOutput of this command must be single email address per line.\n"
"\tDefault is the value of 'sendemail.toCmd' configuration value.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:326
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--cc-cmd=<command>::`\n"
"\tSpecify a command to execute once per patch file which\n"
"\tshould generate patch file specific \"Cc:\" entries.\n"
"\tOutput of this command must be single email address per line.\n"
"\tDefault is the value of `sendemail.ccCmd` configuration value.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:334
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--header-cmd=<command>::`\n"
"\tSpecify a command that is executed once per outgoing message\n"
"\tand output RFC 2822 style header lines to be inserted into\n"
"\tthem. When the `sendemail.headerCmd` configuration variable is\n"
"\tset, its value is always used. When --header-cmd is provided\n"
"\tat the command line, its value takes precedence over the\n"
"\t`sendemail.headerCmd` configuration variable.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:337
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--no-header-cmd::`\n"
"\tDisable any header command in use.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:345
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--[no-]chain-reply-to::`\n"
"\tIf this is set, each email will be sent as a reply to the previous\n"
"\temail sent.  If disabled with \"--no-chain-reply-to\", all emails after\n"
"\tthe first will be sent as replies to the first email sent.  When using\n"
"\tthis, it is recommended that the first file given be an overview of the\n"
"\tentire patch series. Disabled by default, but the "
"`sendemail.chainReplyTo`\n"
"\tconfiguration variable can be used to enable it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:351
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--identity=<identity>::`\n"
"\tA configuration identity. When given, causes values in the\n"
"\t'sendemail.<identity>' subsection to take precedence over\n"
"\tvalues in the 'sendemail' section. The default identity is\n"
"\tthe value of `sendemail.identity`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:356
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--[no-]signed-off-by-cc::`\n"
"\tIf this is set, add emails found in the `Signed-off-by` trailer or Cc: "
"lines to the\n"
"\tcc list. Default is the value of `sendemail.signedOffByCc` configuration\n"
"\tvalue; if that is unspecified, default to --signed-off-by-cc.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:362
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--[no-]cc-cover::`\n"
"\tIf this is set, emails found in Cc: headers in the first patch of\n"
"\tthe series (typically the cover letter) are added to the cc list\n"
"\tfor each email set. Default is the value of 'sendemail.ccCover'\n"
"\tconfiguration value; if that is unspecified, default to --no-cc-cover.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:368
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--[no-]to-cover::`\n"
"\tIf this is set, emails found in To: headers in the first patch of\n"
"\tthe series (typically the cover letter) are added to the to list\n"
"\tfor each email set. Default is the value of 'sendemail.toCover'\n"
"\tconfiguration value; if that is unspecified, default to --no-to-cover.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:372
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--suppress-cc=<category>::`\n"
"\tSpecify an additional category of recipients to suppress the\n"
"\tauto-cc of:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:375
msgid "'author' will avoid including the patch author."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:376
msgid "'self' will avoid including the sender."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:378
msgid ""
"'cc' will avoid including anyone mentioned in Cc lines in the patch header "
"except for self (use 'self' for that)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:380
msgid ""
"'bodycc' will avoid including anyone mentioned in Cc lines in the patch body "
"(commit message) except for self (use 'self' for that)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:382
msgid ""
"'sob' will avoid including anyone mentioned in the Signed-off-by trailers "
"except for self (use 'self' for that)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:385
msgid ""
"'misc-by' will avoid including anyone mentioned in Acked-by, Reviewed-by, "
"Tested-by and other \"-by\" lines in the patch body, except Signed-off-by "
"(use 'sob' for that)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:386
msgid "'cccmd' will avoid running the --cc-cmd."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:387
msgid "'body' is equivalent to 'sob' + 'bodycc' + 'misc-by'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:388
msgid "'all' will suppress all auto cc values."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:393
msgid ""
"Default is the value of `sendemail.suppressCc` configuration value; if that "
"is unspecified, default to 'self' if --suppress-from is specified, as well "
"as 'body' if --no-signed-off-cc is specified."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:398
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--[no-]suppress-from::`\n"
"\tIf this is set, do not add the From: address to the cc: list.\n"
"\tDefault is the value of `sendemail.suppressFrom` configuration\n"
"\tvalue; if that is unspecified, default to --no-suppress-from.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:405
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--[no-]thread::`\n"
"\tIf this is set, the In-Reply-To and References headers will be\n"
"\tadded to each email sent.  Whether each mail refers to the\n"
"\tprevious email (`deep` threading per 'git format-patch'\n"
"\twording) or to the first email (`shallow` threading) is\n"
"\tgoverned by \"--[no-]chain-reply-to\".\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:410
msgid ""
"If disabled with \"--no-thread\", those headers will not be added (unless "
"specified with --in-reply-to).  Default is the value of the "
"`sendemail.thread` configuration value; if that is unspecified, default to "
"--thread."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:416
msgid ""
"It is up to the user to ensure that no In-Reply-To header already exists "
"when 'git send-email' is asked to add it (especially note that 'git "
"format-patch' can be configured to do the threading itself).  Failure to do "
"so may not produce the expected result in the recipient's MUA."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:423
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--[no-]mailmap::`\n"
"\tUse the mailmap file (see linkgit:gitmailmap[5]) to map all\n"
"\taddresses to their canonical real name and email address. Additional\n"
"\tmailmap data specific to git-send-email may be provided using the\n"
"\t`sendemail.mailmap.file` or `sendemail.mailmap.blob` configuration\n"
"\tvalues. Defaults to `sendemail.mailmap`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:425
#, no-wrap
msgid "Administering"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:429
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--confirm=<mode>::`\n"
"\tConfirm just before sending:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:432
msgid "'always' will always confirm before sending"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:433
msgid "'never' will never confirm before sending"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:435
msgid ""
"'cc' will confirm before sending when send-email has automatically added "
"addresses from the patch to the Cc list"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:436
msgid ""
"'compose' will confirm before sending the first message when using "
"--compose."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:437
msgid "'auto' is equivalent to 'cc' + 'compose'"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:442
msgid ""
"Default is the value of `sendemail.confirm` configuration value; if that is "
"unspecified, default to 'auto' unless any of the suppress options have been "
"specified, in which case default to 'compose'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:445
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--dry-run::`\n"
"\tDo everything except actually send the emails.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:451
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--[no-]format-patch::`\n"
"\tWhen an argument may be understood either as a reference or as a file "
"name,\n"
"\tchoose to understand it as a format-patch argument (`--format-patch`)\n"
"\tor as a file name (`--no-format-patch`). By default, when such a "
"conflict\n"
"\toccurs, git send-email will fail.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:455
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--quiet::`\n"
"\tMake git-send-email less verbose.  One line per email should be\n"
"\tall that is output.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:459
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--[no-]validate::`\n"
"\tPerform sanity checks on patches.\n"
"\tCurrently, validation means the following:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:462
msgid "Invoke the sendemail-validate hook if present (see linkgit:githooks[5])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:467
msgid ""
"Warn of patches that contain lines longer than 998 characters unless a "
"suitable transfer encoding ('auto', 'base64', or 'quoted-printable') is "
"used; this is due to SMTP limits as described by "
"https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc5322.txt."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:471
msgid ""
"Default is the value of `sendemail.validate`; if this is not set, default to "
"`--validate`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:474
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--force::`\n"
"\tSend emails even if safety checks would prevent it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:477
#, no-wrap
msgid "Information"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:484
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--dump-aliases::`\n"
"\tInstead of the normal operation, dump the shorthand alias names from\n"
"\tthe configured alias file(s), one per line in alphabetical order. Note\n"
"\tthat this only includes the alias name and not its expanded email "
"addresses.\n"
"\tSee 'sendemail.aliasesFile' for more information about aliases.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:491
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--translate-aliases::`\n"
"\tInstead of the normal operation, read from standard input and\n"
"\tinterpret each line as an email alias. Translate it according to the\n"
"\tconfigured alias file(s). Output each translated name and email\n"
"\taddress to standard output, one per line. See 'sendemail.aliasFile'\n"
"\tfor more information about aliases.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:493
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONFIGURATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:500
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXAMPLES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ~
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:502
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use gmail as the smtp server"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:505
msgid ""
"To use 'git send-email' to send your patches through the GMail SMTP server, "
"edit ~/.gitconfig to specify your account settings:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:512
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[sendemail]\n"
"\tsmtpEncryption = tls\n"
"\tsmtpServer = smtp.gmail.com\n"
"\tsmtpUser = yourname@gmail.com\n"
"\tsmtpServerPort = 587\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:517
msgid ""
"If you have multi-factor authentication set up on your Gmail account, you "
"can generate an app-specific password for use with 'git send-email'. Visit "
"https://security.google.com/settings/security/apppasswords to create it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:520
msgid ""
"Once your commits are ready to be sent to the mailing list, run the "
"following commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:524
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t$ git format-patch --cover-letter -M origin/master -o outgoing/\n"
"\t$ edit outgoing/0000-*\n"
"\t$ git send-email outgoing/*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:529
msgid ""
"The first time you run it, you will be prompted for your credentials.  Enter "
"the app-specific or your regular password as appropriate.  If you have "
"credential helper configured (see linkgit:git-credential[1]), the password "
"will be saved in the credential store so you won't have to type it the next "
"time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-send-email.txt:535
msgid ""
"Note: the following core Perl modules that may be installed with your "
"distribution of Perl are required: MIME::Base64, MIME::QuotedPrint, "
"Net::Domain and Net::SMTP.  These additional Perl modules are also required: "
"Authen::SASL and Mail::Address."
msgstr ""

